# GridScribe deploy environment - template for the VPS copy.
#
# Copy to /etc/gridscribe/deploy.env on the VPS and fill in the blanks:
#   sudo install -d -m 755 /etc/gridscribe
#   sudo cp scripts/deploy.env.example /etc/gridscribe/deploy.env
#   sudo $EDITOR /etc/gridscribe/deploy.env
#   sudo chown root:root /etc/gridscribe/deploy.env && sudo chmod 600 /etc/gridscribe/deploy.env
#
# A filled-in copy is never committed - scripts/deploy.env* is git-ignored.
#
# EVERY value here is empty on purpose, and src/lib/config/deploy-script-vars.test.ts
# fails CI if any of them stops being empty. An empty optional value turns that feature
# off. An empty REQUIRED value makes deploy.sh refuse to deploy, which is the point:
# ORIGIN and PUBLIC_ALLOWED_ORIGINS have to name the domain THIS host serves, and
# nothing in the deploy can work that out on its own. A template that carried
# gridfinitylabels.com would let a fork deploy at its own domain, pass every check
# against the committed value, and still 403 its own front end.
#
# scripts/deploy.sh SOURCES this file, so ordinary shell quoting works - and so the
# file must be root-owned and not group/world writable. It is for the app's environment
# only: an assignment to one of the script's own options (TAG, DRY_RUN, CHECK_ONLY,
# DO_PULL, ENV_FILE) is refused, because sourcing would let it overrule the command
# line.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required. deploy.sh refuses to deploy while either is empty or malformed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Public URL of the site, as visitors reach it. A bare origin: scheme://host, no
# trailing slash, no path, and no default port (:443 on https, :80 on http) - a browser
# leaves the default port out, so deploy.sh refuses an explicit one. SvelteKit
# adapter-node resolves request URLs with it.
#
#   ORIGIN="https://labels.example.org"
ORIGIN=""

# Comma-separated origins allowed to POST /api/shorten - the QR URL shortener.
#
# Each entry must be a bare origin, with no trailing slash and no path, because it is
# compared against the browser's Origin header character for character (lowercased)
# in src/lib/utils/api-security.ts. "https://labels.example.org/" with a trailing
# slash fails exactly as silently as a missing value. localhost dev origins are
# always allowed and do not belong here.
#
# List every hostname the site answers on, apex and www alike. deploy.sh probes the
# running container once per entry and refuses the deploy if any entry is rejected.
#
# The value of ORIGIN above MUST appear in this list. If it does not, the site's own
# QR shortener answers 403 and every QR code silently carries the full long URL
# instead of a short one. deploy.sh checks this and refuses to start.
#
#   PUBLIC_ALLOWED_ORIGINS="https://labels.example.org,https://www.labels.example.org"
PUBLIC_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional and operator-specific. An empty value turns the feature off, and deploy.sh
# lists which ones are off on every run. A fork that copies this template unedited must
# not report to someone else's analytics or publish someone else's contact details.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Analytics. Both must be set for tracking to be active. Point them at YOUR OWN
# Matomo instance. IP anonymization must be enabled in the Matomo admin - the app
# does not enforce it.
PUBLIC_MATOMO_URL=""
PUBLIC_MATOMO_SITE_ID=""

# Amazon Associates. Empty hides the affiliate links.
PUBLIC_AMAZON_STORE_ID=""
PUBLIC_AFFILIATE_PTE560BT=""
PUBLIC_AFFILIATE_PTP710BT=""
PUBLIC_AFFILIATE_TZE231=""
PUBLIC_AFFILIATE_MAGNETS=""

# Shown in the in-app privacy policy. Empty renders a neutral self-hosted notice.
PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=""
PUBLIC_PRIVACY_CONTROLLER=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never enabled in production.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLIC_ALLOW_E2E_PAGES exposes the internal /e2e render-comparison routes on the
# public site. deploy.sh refuses to deploy when it is "true", and pins it to false in
# the container, so it is deliberately absent from this file.
